Subject: [PATCH] cgroup, sched: preserve android12-5.10 KMI with CPU and PID limits

Target: android12-5.10 GKI (Linux 5.10.236, KMI generation 9)
Verified base: android12-5.10-2025-05 (71f3aedc8b92dec66ff028df25fe9ddfeafea88c)
Frozen configuration: CONFIG_CFS_BANDWIDTH=n, CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=n
Required configuration: CONFIG_CFS_BANDWIDTH=y, CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y

Port of fix_cgroup_limits_kabi_5.15.167.patch to android12-5.10.

Keep the frozen subsystem IDs and ABI-visible cgroup arrays unchanged when
enabling PIDS. The pids controller is placed behind all other subsystems;
css_set and cgroup keep the array sizes of the frozen KMI
(CGROUP_SUBSYS_KABI_COUNT) and the pids state lives in extension objects that
are allocated directly behind struct ext_css_set, behind a cgroup (after
ancestor_ids[]) or behind a cgroup_root. Subsystem and e_cset access goes
through helper functions.

Move CFS bandwidth runtime state from inline cfs_rq fields into separately
allocated cfs_rq_bandwidth objects (allocated behind each group cfs_rq, per
CPU static storage for the root cfs_rq). The per task group state becomes a
separately allocated cfs_bandwidth_state, pointed to by task_group
ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(2) via ANDROID_KABI_USE(2). The pointer in struct cfs_rq
sits in the tail padding behind android_vendor_data1, so offsets and
sizeof() of struct cfs_rq and struct rq are unchanged. New members are hidden
from genksyms so that symbol version CRCs stay identical.

Differences from the 5.15 patch: no pids_ext_low/high fields in css_set (the
extension is found by address), cfs_rq pointer in padding instead of in the
middle of the struct, destroy_cfs_bandwidth() tolerates a not yet allocated
state, CFS bandwidth burst does not exist in 5.10.

Enable the required options in the target kernel configuration separately;
this patch does not modify a defconfig. It must not be applied to a KMI that
was frozen with either option enabled, or to a tree that already uses
task_group KABI reserve 2.

